    "teacher_markdown": "For Teachers Only\r\n\r\nExpected output:\r\nSong 1: 3 min\r\nSong 2: 4 min\r\nSong 3: 5 min\r\nSong 4: 6 min\r\nSong 5: 7 min\r\nTotal: 25 min\r\nAverage: 5.0 min\r\n\r\nDo not explain the result yet. Students investigate this same pattern in Level 2.\r\n\r\nWatch for: students are surprised that the average prints as 5.0, not 5. Division in Python gives a decimal. Accept this and move on. Students who predict the songs start at 1 or that j is the song length are tracing j instead of 3 + j. Ask them to write j's value for each pass.\r\n\r\nj ends at 4 but the program never prints it, so do not ask students for j's last value on this level."
